<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<coreProperties xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/metadata/core-properties">
  <dc:creator>Israel Iyonsi</dc:creator>
  <dc:description>Cross-platform filename and path validation and sanitization for .NET: the pathvalidate for .NET. Turn any user-supplied name into a safe filename that will not break, overwrite, or open a path-traversal hole. Handles the traps hand-rolled Path.GetInvalidFileNameChars() loops miss: Windows reserved device names (CON, PRN, AUX, NUL, COM1-9, LPT1-9, including with any extension and case-insensitively), trailing dots and spaces (which Windows silently strips), UTF-8 byte length limits (not just character counts), control characters, DEL, path separators, and the reserved characters that differ per platform. Per-platform profiles (Windows, POSIX, Universal, Auto), extension-preserving length truncation, configurable replacement, reserved-name policy, and a detailed Validate API with per-error reasons and positions. Sanitize never throws on the input name and its output is guaranteed to pass Validate for the same profile. Includes a full-path sanitizer that neutralizes traversal and rejoins with the platform separator. Zero external dependencies.</dc:description>
  <dc:identifier>SafeName</dc:identifier>
  <version>0.1.1</version>
  <keywords>filename path sanitize validation filesystem upload security cross-platform pathvalidate slug</keywords>
  <lastModifiedBy>NuGet.Build.Tasks.Pack, Version=6.11.2.1, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=31bf3856ad364e35;.NET Standard 2.0</lastModifiedBy>
</coreProperties>